L66: 				\begin{document}$$\dot{V}{\text{O}}_{2\max }$$\end{document} V ˙ O 2 max . Similarly, improved markers of mitochondrial adaptations (such as mitochondrial enzyme activity, PGC1-alpha content and mitochondrial DNA levels) following endurance training plus protein feeding have not been consistently reported (Ferguson-Stegall et al.  2011 ; Knuiman et al.  2019 ; Robinson et al.  2011 ). Inclusion of other potentially active ingredients such as caffeine and flavonoids (Ferguson-Stegall et al.  2011 ); selection of a control group not matched for macronutrient/energy content (Okazaki et al.  2009 ; Roberson et al.  2018 ); lack of double blinding (Ferguson-Stegall et al.  2011 ; Roberson et al.  2018 ); and insufficient sample size (Roberson et al.  2018 ; Robinson et al.  2011 ) make it difficult to conclude on the role of protein feeding in endurance training adaptations. Only two running-based studies were conducted, which did not measure  \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
